UID:eaafe85ba894e3d5d7ddc8f9b0703b1c8192026_10:22:03_AM@campusgroups.com
SUMMARY;ENCODING=QUOTED-PRINTABLE:F1RST Families Welcome Lunch
LOCATION: Sign in to download the location
URL:https://terriercentral.bu.edu/rsvp?id=375451
DESCRIPTION:Please note this event is intended for first year, first-generation undergrad students who are moving in for Orientation and their families.\n\nWelcome to Boston University, F1RST Families!\n\nCome take a break from the hustle and bustle of move-in to meet the Newbury Center staff and explore our space. We’re so excited to meet you!\n\nWhat does it mean to be first-generation at Boston University?\n\nFirst-Generation College Student (FGCS):\n\nA student in the first generation of their family to go to college (i.e., a student whose parents/guardians/caregivers did not earn bachelor’s degrees, although elder siblings and cousins may be attending college already or have earned four-year degrees).\n---\nEvent Details: https://terriercentral.bu.edu/rsvp?id=375451
END:VEVENT
