UID:fade9eaef4998330e6d02c2f850d6ec98192026_11:43:53_AM@campusgroups.com
SUMMARY;ENCODING=QUOTED-PRINTABLE:Newbury Center First-Gen Virtual Orientation
LOCATION:Online Event
URL:https://terriercentral.bu.edu/rsvp?id=375456
DESCRIPTION:If you're unable to attend one of our in-person sessions, our First-Gen Virtual Orientation is for you!\n \nOpen to first-gen students at all BU campus locations, this orientation will be held on Zoom, allowing you to attend from anywhere. Join us to learn about the Newbury Center, upcoming events, and to meet fellow first-gen students and start building your Terrier F1RSTS community!\n\nTo receive the Zoom link, please register using the link.\n\nWhat does it mean to be first-generation at Boston University?\n\nFirst-Generation College Student (FGCS):\n\nA student in the first generation of their family to go to college (i.e., a student whose parents/guardians/caregivers did not earn bachelor’s degrees, although elder siblings and cousins may be attending college already or have earned four-year degrees).\n\nFirst-Generation Graduate/Professional Student (FGGS/FGPS):\n\nA student who is in the first-generation of their families to pursue an advanced degree (i.e., a student whose parents/guardians/caregivers did not earn a master’s, doctorate, or professional degree, such as a JD or MD).\n\nMeeting Link: https://bostonu.zoom.us/meeting/register/6N73GCM5RKmf9VHzqLHePQ#/registration\n---\nEvent Details: https://terriercentral.bu.edu/rsvp?id=375456
END:VEVENT
