UID:8186644a013671ba74d07846b664dd038192026_2:54:10_PM@campusgroups.com
SUMMARY;ENCODING=QUOTED-PRINTABLE:Terrier F1RSTS Library Orientation
LOCATION: Sign in to download the location
URL:https://terriercentral.bu.edu/rsvp?id=375474
DESCRIPTION:BU Libraries has countless resources to support you during your academic journey. If you're performing research, writing a paper, or something in between, BU Libraries is here to help.\n\nJoin us on Tuesday, September 15 for an introduction to BU Libraries designed specifically for our Terrier F1RSTS!\n\nPizza will be served, so please register in advance.\n\nThe intended audience is BU first-generation students. \n\nWhat does it mean to be first-generation undergrad, graduate, and professional students at Boston University?\n\nFirst-Generation College Student (FGCS):\n\nA student in the first generation of their family to go to college (i.e., a student whose parents/guardians/caregivers did not earn bachelor’s degrees, although elder siblings and cousins may be attending college already or have earned four-year degrees).\n\nFirst-Generation Graduate/Professional Student (FGGS/FGPS):\n\nA student who is in the first-generation of their families to pursue an advanced degree (i.e., a student whose parents/guardians/caregivers did not earn a master’s, doctorate, or professional degree, such as a JD or MD).\n---\nEvent Details: https://terriercentral.bu.edu/rsvp?id=375474
END:VEVENT
