UID:0478fc3cae56c3d565d0ea609d0a2a1f8202026_4:43:28_PM@campusgroups.com
SUMMARY;ENCODING=QUOTED-PRINTABLE:Pre-Health Pop Up for First-Gen Students
LOCATION: Sign in to download the location
URL:https://terriercentral.bu.edu/rsvp?id=375548
DESCRIPTION:Join Pre-Health Advisors at a Pre-health Pop-Up Near You! We're hosting Pop-Up advising sessions at various campus locations you frequent most, offering a convenient opportunity to meet with our advisors. \n\nIn this informal, group office-hour format, you can discuss your most pressing pre-health questions and get personalized guidance. \n\nTo make the most of your time, we recommend completing the "Introduction to the Pre-Health Pathway" module before attending. The module is accessible via our Pre-health 101 Blackboard site.\n\nWhat does it mean to be first-generation at Boston University?\n\nFirst-Generation College Student (FGCS):\n\nA student in the first generation of their family to go to college (i.e., a student whose parents/guardians/caregivers did not earn bachelor’s degrees, although elder siblings and cousins may be attending college already or have earned four-year degrees).\n\nFirst-Generation Graduate/Professional Student (FGGS/FGPS):\n\nA student who is in the first-generation of their families to pursue an advanced degree (i.e., a student whose parents/guardians/caregivers did not earn a master’s, doctorate, or professional degree, such as a JD or MD).\n---\nEvent Details: https://terriercentral.bu.edu/rsvp?id=375548
END:VEVENT
