UID:befa33a4ed8ec6f0aefe02b1eb74765c8132026_5:48:37_PM@campusgroups.com
SUMMARY;ENCODING=QUOTED-PRINTABLE:Carnival Latino
LOCATION: Sign in to download the location
URL:https://terriercentral.bu.edu/rsvp?id=375318
DESCRIPTION:Carnival Latino (formerly known as Festival Latino) is our first major event of the year making it one of the most important. This event will be our final event for the month of September, which is also Hispanic Heritage Month. Hispanic Heritage Month is tremendously important to the Hispanic community and BU students alike. As the biggest Latinx Association on campus we will hold Festival Latino to gather all Latinx clubs and its members here at BU and give them a space to interact with one another and celebrate the Hispanic community. Additionally, the process of meeting people and finding your home away from home can often be overwhelming. We hope to minimize the hassle by allowing new BU students from all organizations to catch a glimpse of the Latino community in a fun and informative way. At this event we not only invite other BU clubs but also host local Latino artists from the greater Boston area to perform along with some performances from dance groups on campus like Sabor Latino. Tickets will cost $5 dollars to BU students. We will open this event to non-BU students as well, charging them $7 each to attend. The food will be from the beloved Guatemalan restaurant chain, Pollo Campero, and the variety of activities such as face paint, carnival outdoor games, and piñata will be representative of a traditional Latino festival. By holding this event, we hope to encourage students to meet and join our Latinx clubs regardless of background to celebrate Hispanic heritage and embark their BU journey with a strong support system! \n---\nEvent Details: https://terriercentral.bu.edu/rsvp?id=375318
END:VEVENT
