UID:6d42ca30ebb5e1fb50984e90188fb69e9132026_1:32:36_PM@campusgroups.com
SUMMARY;ENCODING=QUOTED-PRINTABLE:Enterprise 5.0
LOCATION:Howard Thurman Center, 808 Commonwealth Avenue, Boston, MA 02215, United States
URL:https://terriercentral.bu.edu/rsvp?id=376434
DESCRIPTION:This program will bring back an Epsilon Chapter and Sigma Chapter of Alpha Phi Alpha Fraternity, Incorporated tradition started in Fall 2011 and follow the College Life to Corporate Life Initiative (C2C) and Economic Growth & Success initiatives. The program will focus on preparing students for life after graduation by exploring what it means to navigate corporate spaces as Black professionals while building the skills and connections necessary for long term career and financial success through a panel. The panel will be made up of professionals from a variety of industries to share their experiences. At the end, attendees will participate in a structured network session to engage in meaningful conversations.\n---\nEvent Details: https://terriercentral.bu.edu/rsvp?id=376434
END:VEVENT
