UID:d527a3cd2c6682f0e9de39787ab96c6f9132026_2:06:30_PM@campusgroups.com
SUMMARY;ENCODING=QUOTED-PRINTABLE:Every Voice Speaks
LOCATION: Sign in to download the location
URL:https://terriercentral.bu.edu/rsvp?id=376439
DESCRIPTION:This program will promote voter participation, civic engagement, and Black political empowerment through the A Voteless People Is A Hopeless People and Foster the Future: From Here to Hope initiatives. The first portion of the program will consist of voter registration and voter education tabling in a low-income community in either Mattapan or Dorchester. Members will help community residents register to vote and provide accessible voter education resources. The evening program, Beyond the Ballot, will focus on civic engagement within the Black community beyond voting. Attendees will learn about additional ways to create change within their communities, including advocacy, contacting elected officials, attending public meetings, community organizing, serving on local boards and commissions, and other forms of civic participation. The program will emphasize that voting is an important component of civic engagement while encouraging attendees to remain involved in their communities beyond Election Day.\n---\nEvent Details: https://terriercentral.bu.edu/rsvp?id=376439
END:VEVENT
