UID:11b0a1cd452f28210803356b32613a0a1062026_12:36:48_PM@campusgroups.com
SUMMARY;ENCODING=QUOTED-PRINTABLE:October Town Hall
LOCATION:PHO 906, 775 Commonwealth Ave B43, Boston, MA 02215, United States
URL:https://terriercentral.bu.edu/rsvp?id=377535
DESCRIPTION:The Student Government Town Hall is a single-day event held once a month during the last week of each month and typically lasts one hour. Each session is scheduled for the evening to maximize accessibility, with an expected attendance of 50-75 students depending on the month and topic. The event features catered food, an informational presentation from the Sexual Assault Prevention Department, introductions from SARP, BU Police, and Student Health Services, and a structured discussion format that includes moderated questions and open student Q&A. The most important features of the Town Halls are their consistency, accessibility through rotating weekdays, and the opportunity for direct dialogue between students and decision-makers, ensuring that student perspectives are heard and acted upon.\n---\nEvent Details: https://terriercentral.bu.edu/rsvp?id=377535
END:VEVENT
