UID:0b79afdf2bedea5edd58652e502326178192026_2:51:49_PM@campusgroups.com
SUMMARY;ENCODING=QUOTED-PRINTABLE:Fuel Up Friday for the First-Gen Community
LOCATION: Sign in to download the location
URL:https://terriercentral.bu.edu/rsvp?id=375472
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a light breakfast of coffee, tea, fruit, yogurt, and an Einstein Bagel from 9 to 11 a.m. in the Newbury Center. \n\nNo registration is needed, so feel free to drop in any time during the event hours. Whether you're heading to class or looking for somewhere to meet up with your Terrier F1RSTS community, First-Gen Fuel Up Friday is the perfect opportunity.\n\nThis is one of our most popular events, so the food is first-come, first-serve. We recommend coming early for the best chance of getting your choice of a bagel. See you there!\n\nThe intended audience is BU first-generation undergraduate, graduate, and professional students.\n\nWhat does it mean to be first-generation at Boston University?\n\nFirst-Generation College Student (FGCS):\n\nA student in the first generation of their family to go to college (i.e., a student whose parents/guardians/caregivers did not earn bachelor’s degrees, although elder siblings and cousins may be attending college already or have earned four-year degrees).\n\nFirst-Generation Graduate/Professional Student (FGGS/FGPS):\n\nA student who is in the first-generation of their families to pursue an advanced degree (i.e., a student whose parents/guardians/caregivers did not earn a master’s, doctorate, or professional degree, such as a JD or MD).\n---\nEvent Details: https://terriercentral.bu.edu/rsvp?id=375472
END:VEVENT
